{
  "_comment": [
    "Per-team light and dark palettes, mirroring the .t-* classes in design/reference.html.",
    "fill_hex = --tf (badge/button/pill/thumbnail fill and the hero glow; SAME in both themes).",
    "on_fill_hex = --on (text drawn on top of fill_hex; #FFFFFF everywhere, as in the reference).",
    "primary_light_hex / primary_dark_hex = --t (accent for text and small marks).",
    "secondary_light_hex / secondary_dark_hex = --t2 (rings and borders).",
    "source 'reference' rows are copied verbatim from design/reference.html and must not be recomputed.",
    "source 'hand_tuned' rows are authored in the same style. Dark variants are hand-tuned, never",
    "computed (SPEC.md 5.1, 8.2): a lighter, higher-chroma version of the team colour that still reads",
    "as the team. Every primary_light_hex clears 4.5:1 on the light screen (#FFFFFF) and every",
    "primary_dark_hex clears 4.5:1 on the dark screen (#0E1115); check with",
    "python3 seed/scripts/check_team_colors.py."
  ],
